WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.259
Suicide Squad was one of the highest-grossing
releases of 2016, setting a new record for

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:10.540
the best ever opening weekend in August and
going on to earn $745 million worldwide.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:16.270
Critics, however, tore it apart, calling it,
quote, "slipshod" and "a patched-together

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.020
mess," among other things.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.480
So how sloppy is Suicide Squad?

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.980
Here are just a few examples.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.039
“Worst part of it is they’re gonna blame
us for the whole thing.”

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:27.300
Name changer

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.460
Near the start of the film, a character clearly
identified as Admiral Mackenzie isn't sold

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.660
on the idea of Task Force X.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.370
Or is it Admiral Olsen?

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.489
Ted Whittall's character wears a name tag
identifying him as Mackenzie, which can be

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:43.930
seen several times throughout the scene.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:49.000
But bizarrely, when the end credits roll,
his character is listed as Admiral Olsen.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.110
It was a nice touch to bring Whittall on board
— hardcore DC fans will remember him as

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:57.570
Suicide Squad leader Rick Flag in the final
season of Smallville — but the confusion

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:02.579
over his character's name shows how little
importance he actually had in the script.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:04.079
Traveling light

00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:09.390
After extorting his client for an extra million
dollars and carrying out a near-impossible

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:14.090
hit, Deadshot makes his escape by jumping
over the edge of the building and rappelling

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.090
down the wall.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:19.110
But before he makes a run for it, he grabs
his big bag of high-tech gear.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:23.119
But what happens next sticks out like a sore
thumb, once you know about it.

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:27.340
The rucksack he scoops up as he sprints for
the ledge is nowhere to be seen while he's

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.830
actually descending — it just disappears
into thin air.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.170
“That’s how I cut and run.”

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.350
Kiddie pool

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.820
When The Joker dives headfirst into the same
vat of chemicals as his beloved Harley Quinn,

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.430
there's something off about the staging.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:45.380
“Would you die for me?”

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.829
“Yes.”

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:51.180
We see from other shots of the vats, and shots
from below the surface of the chemicals, that

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.850
the containers are pretty deep.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.120
It's definitely deep enough for a person to
jump into it from a great height and not be

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:57.920
killed.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.320
“That's too easy.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.660
Would you...

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.780
Would you live for me?”

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:12.120
Yet after the Joker jumps in to rescue Quinn,
he's able to cradle her in his arms and kiss

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.370
her while standing still, which is impossible
— unless he suddenly developed Aquaman-like

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.740
swimming powers.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.580
[laughing]

00:02:21.529 --> 00:02:22.939
Magic highlights

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:27.720
Harley Quinn is captured by Batman when a
sportscar she's in, driven by the Joker, goes

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.599
crashing into the harbor.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:33.999
Wanting to take them both alive, the Caped
Crusader goes in after them, where he finds

00:02:33.999 --> 00:02:36.160
the Joker missing and Quinn unconscious.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.609
“Stupid bat, you’re ruining date night!”

00:02:39.609 --> 00:02:44.030
Underwater, Quinn's hair is entirely blonde,
free from the pink and blue highlights she

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.280
sports for the majority of the movie.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:50.909
After Batman pulls her from the water, however,
the highlights inexplicably return.

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:52.389
Moone's mistakes

00:02:52.389 --> 00:02:57.250
June Moone is an archaeologist who finds a
totem containing an evil spirit in an ancient

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:01.319
Peruvian temple and is possessed by it, becoming
the Enchantress.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:06.730
In one scene, Enchantress obtains a binder
from the Weapons Ministry Vault in Tehran.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.999
Written in Persian script, it should open
and be read right-to-left, instead of left-to-right.

00:03:11.999 --> 00:03:14.129
But Suicide Squad gets it backwards.

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:18.629
In a later scene, we can see Moone is holding
a beer bottle in her hand as she fiddles with

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:19.889
Rick Flag's shirt.

00:03:19.889 --> 00:03:24.879
The angle changes as Moone leans in for a
kiss, and now the bottle is somehow in his

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.540
hand.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.860
“I saw it move!”

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.160
Elevator edits

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:34.820
During an error-laden elevator ascent, Harley
Quinn is attacked by one of Enchantress' foot

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:39.489
soldiers, who drops down into the elevator
by removing a panel in the ceiling.

00:03:39.489 --> 00:03:43.370
Quinn dispatches it with a bullet to the head
and then a second attacker smashes through

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.469
the window.

00:03:44.469 --> 00:03:50.139
Two glaring mistakes follow: First, the body
of the creature she shot dead seconds earlier

00:03:50.139 --> 00:03:51.439
just vanishes.

00:03:51.439 --> 00:03:57.040
Then, during the second fight, Quinn runs
up the wall and flips over her assailant,

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.529
and when she does, we get a shot of the elevator
ceiling.

00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:04.049
The panel that was removed moments ago is
now back in place.

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:07.219
A bad day at the office for the editing team.

00:04:07.219 --> 00:04:08.709
Peeping toms

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:12.529
There's another Harley Quinn-related goof
during the scene in which the Squad get out

00:04:12.529 --> 00:04:14.829
of their prison rags and get suited up.

00:04:14.829 --> 00:04:18.919
As she slips into something a little more
comfortable, the camera pans up Margot Robbie's

00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:22.990
body slowly as if to mimic the leering of
the men nearby.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:28.061
Hardly anyone is around Quinn as she squeezes
into her "Daddy's Lil Monster" t-shirt, yet

00:04:28.061 --> 00:04:31.590
in the next shot, she's suddenly surrounded
by gawking men.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:34.620
A funny reveal, but it makes zero sense.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.620
"What?"

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.620
Thanks for watching!

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.010
